-All API requests expect `amount` values in the currency’s _minor unit_ (The Stripe API expects currency values using the given denomination's smallest unit represented without decimals. For example, enter 1099 to charge 10.99 USD (or any other two-decimal currency). Enter 10 to charge 10 JPY (or any other zero-decimal currency)). Use the rates provided by the [FX Quotes API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/fx_quotes.md), and convert the resulting amount into Stripe [minor units](https://docs.stripe.com/currencies.md#minor-units). Learn more about [zero-decimal currencies](https://docs.stripe.com/currencies.md#zero-decimal).
+### Handle minor units 
+
+All API requests expect `amount` values in the currency’s *minor unit* (The Stripe API expects currency values using the given denomination's smallest unit represented without decimals. For example, enter 1099 to charge 10.99 USD (or any other two-decimal currency). Enter 10 to charge 10 JPY (or any other zero-decimal currency)). Use the rates provided by the [FX Quotes API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/fx_quotes.md), and convert the resulting amount into Stripe [minor units](https://docs.stripe.com/currencies.md#minor-units). Learn more about [zero-decimal currencies](https://docs.stripe.com/currencies.md#zero-decimal).
 
